		practice: {
			id: 'data-sql-items',
			title: 'A table of services and queries on it',
			task: 'The page has six boxes for queries. 1) Create the items table: at every “…” write the column’s type (serial with PRIMARY KEY suits id, text NOT NULL suits the title, integer suits the price). 2) Add at least five rows, each in parentheses on its own line; take the titles from your own services. 3) Write a SELECT with WHERE, ORDER BY and LIMIT. 4) Write a query with GROUP BY and COUNT that counts the items by category. 5) Change the price of one record with UPDATE and 6) delete another with DELETE, both with WHERE. 7) In the last line, say which query is dangerous without WHERE. The checks read the text of your queries; you see the results under the boxes in the preview. Every “…” has to be replaced.',
			era: 3,
			files: {
				'index.html': `<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
